From: Flavio Fisicaro <flavio@fisicaro.xyz>
Date: 2026-10-31
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: iris: remaining SM8150 VPU5 deltas

Upstream nabu/7.3.y now carries its own legacy_vpu5 support (LLCC
syscache configuration, firmware buffer-requirements sizes and
hold_count, index-based FTB matching), superseding most of the
original 2026-10-22 SM8150 decode patch carried here. Two findings
from that patch are still missing upstream:

1. The DPB pool is deferred to streaming time, so LOAD_RESOURCES
   arrives with an incomplete buffer set on the legacy firmware.
   Queue the whole capture-side set before streamon for legacy_vpu5.

2. The firmware validates FTB allocations against the linear OUTPUT
   size, slightly larger than the reported DPB (UBWC OUTPUT2) size.
   Size the DPB pool with the larger of the two.

NEEDS ON-DEVICE RETEST: verified by inspection against
nabu/7.3.y @ d3bc957cf96c only; decode must be re-proven on hardware
against the upstream legacy_vpu5 implementation.

Signed-off-by: Flavio Fisicaro <flavio@fisicaro.xyz>
---
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_buffer.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_buffer.c
index cec20368a..38208e64d 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_buffer.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_buffer.c
@@ -497,6 +497,15 @@ static void iris_fill_internal_buf_info(struct iris_inst *inst,
 
 	if (exact_firmware_size) {
 		buffers->size = inst->fw_buffer_sizes[buffer_type];
+		if (buffer_type == BUF_DPB)
+			/*
+			 * The VPU5 firmware validates FTB allocations against
+			 * the linear OUTPUT size, which is slightly larger
+			 * than the UBWC OUTPUT2 size it reports for the
+			 * same DPB pool.
+			 */
+			buffers->size = max(buffers->size,
+					    inst->fw_buffer_sizes[BUF_OUTPUT]);
 		if (buffers->size != calculated_size)
 			dev_dbg(inst->core->dev,
 				"Iris1: buffer type %u using exact firmware size %u instead of calculated %u\n",
@@ -651,7 +660,9 @@ int iris_queue_internal_buffers(struct iris_inst *inst, u32 plane)
 				continue;
 			if (buffer->attr & BUF_ATTR_QUEUED)
 				continue;
-			if (buffer->type == BUF_DPB && inst->state != IRIS_INST_STREAMING) {
+			if (buffer->type == BUF_DPB &&
+			    inst->state != IRIS_INST_STREAMING &&
+			    !inst->core->iris_platform_data->legacy_vpu5) {
 				buffer->attr |= BUF_ATTR_DEFERRED;
 				continue;
 			}
